      "page_title": "Streaming Responses",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is streaming",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Streaming== reads the body chunk by chunk. Large downloads, SSE and NDJSON feeds are **never** loaded into memory whole.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. aiohttp: r.content",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with s.get(url) as r:",
            "  r.raise_for_status()",
            "  src = r.content  # StreamReader",
            "  async for b in src.iter_chunked(",
            "      64 * 1024):",
            "    out(b)"
          ],
          "note": "body stays in the socket, not RAM"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Reader",
            "Gives",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`iter_chunked(n)`",
              "fixed-size bytes",
              "files"
            ],
            [
              "`iter_any()`",
              "whatever arrived",
              "low latency"
            ],
            [
              "`readline()`",
              "one line",
              "==line protocols=="
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. httpx: c.stream()",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with c.stream(\"GET\",u) as r:",
            "  r.raise_for_status()",
            "  async for b in r.aiter_bytes():",
            "    out(b)"
          ],
          "note": "c.get() always buffers the FULL body"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Method",
            "Yields"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`aiter_bytes()`",
              "decoded bytes"
            ],
            [
              "`aiter_text()`",
              "str chunks"
            ],
            [
              "`aiter_lines()`",
              "one text line"
            ],
            [
              "`aiter_raw()`",
              "raw, still gzipped"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Rules inside the stream",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`r.raise_for_status()` **before** iterating, so an error page isn't saved as data",
            "`await r.aread()` loads the body on demand, e.g. only on 4xx/5xx",
            "The read timeout is ==per chunk==, so a slow trickle never times out",
            "Hard cap: wrap it in `async with asyncio.timeout(60):`"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Examples: file, feed, upload",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "f = await aiofiles.open(p, \"wb\")",
            "async with c.stream(\"GET\",u) as r:",
            "  r.raise_for_status()",
            "  async for b in r.aiter_bytes():",
            "    await f.write(b)  # no block",
            "await f.close()"
          ],
          "note": "or batch writes via asyncio.to_thread"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with c.stream(\"GET\",u) as r:",
            "  async for ln in r.aiter_lines():",
            "    if ln:  # skip keep-alives",
            "      event = json.loads(ln)"
          ],
          "note": "SSE: strip the 'data: ' prefix first"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`c.get()` on a 2 GB file → httpx **buffers** it all",
            "Half-read stream, never exiting `async with` → connection ==leaked==",
            "Plain `f.write()` in the loop → **blocks** the event loop",
            "No `raise_for_status()` → the 500 HTML page saved as your file",
            "Trusting the read timeout as a total → the download hangs for hours"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Chunks, not whole bodies"
    },
