      "page_title": "Async Web Servers: Handlers & Lifespan",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mechanism: loop vs threadpool"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "FastAPI/Starlette run on an ==ASGI server== ({icon:uvicorn} uvicorn)",
            "**One** event loop per worker process",
            "`async def` endpoint runs ON the loop: await non-blocking I/O only",
            "Plain `def` endpoint runs in the ==anyio threadpool== (40 threads)",
            "So blocking calls are **safe** in `def`, and `def` dependencies go there too"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. aiohttp.web handler"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def handle(request):",
            "    body = await request.json()",
            "    return web.json_response(body)",
            "app.router.add_get('/x', handle)",
            "web.run_app(app)"
          ],
          "note": "handlers MUST be async def"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Path params: `request.match_info['id']` for `/x/{id}`",
            "Body: `await request.json()` (the read is I/O, so await it)",
            "==cleanup_ctx==: code before `yield` runs at startup, code after runs at shutdown"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "S = web.AppKey('s', ClientSession)",
            "async def http_ctx(app):",
            "    app[S] = ClientSession()",
            "    yield",
            "    await app[S].close()",
            "app.cleanup_ctx.append(http_ctx)"
          ],
          "note": "typed AppKey, not a bare string"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. FastAPI lifespan + proxy"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@asynccontextmanager",
            "async def lifespan(app):",
            "    app.state.client = httpx.AsyncClient()",
            "    yield",
            "    await app.state.client.aclose()",
            "app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)"
          ],
          "note": "one client, reused by every request"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def up(c):",
            "  async with c.stream('GET', U) as r:",
            "    async for b in r.aiter_bytes():",
            "      yield b",
            "# endpoint: c = request.app.state.client",
            "return StreamingResponse(up(c))"
          ],
          "note": "proxies upstream without buffering"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Multi-core",
          "items": [
            "`uvicorn app:app --workers N`",
            "`gunicorn -k uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker`",
            "Each worker has **its own** loop and its own lifespan client"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Stuck with sync code?",
          "text": "Offload it with `run_in_threadpool` or `to_thread`, covered on page 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@app.get('/b')",
            "def b():  # runs in threadpool",
            "    r = requests.get(U)",
            "    return r.json()"
          ],
          "note": "safe, but capped at 40 threads"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "fastapi",
      "subtitle": "handlers, lifespan, workers"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Async Server Best Practices",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Server best practices"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async def` only awaits: httpx, asyncpg, `asyncio.sleep`",
            "Blocking library? Plain `def` endpoint or `to_thread`",
            "==One lifespan client== per worker, reused everywhere",
            "Proxy upstream bodies with `StreamingResponse`, **never** buffer"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Deadline on upstream calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@app.get('/p')",
            "async def p(request: Request):",
            "  c = request.app.state.client",
            "  async with asyncio.timeout(5):",
            "    r = await c.get(U)",
            "  return r.json()"
          ],
          "note": "a hung upstream can't hold the handler"
        },
        {
