      "page_title": "Clean Teardown & SIGTERM Handling",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: Clean Teardown",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t = asyncio.create_task(job())",
            "tasks.add(t)  # tasks = set()",
            "t.add_done_callback(tasks.discard)",
            "for t in tasks: t.cancel()",
            "await asyncio.gather(*tasks,",
            "    return_exceptions=True)"
          ],
          "note": "keep refs in a set, cancel, gather"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`wait_for(to_thread(f), 5)`: the **thread** keeps running after timeout",
            "CPU work on threads: GIL means no parallel bytecode",
            "App drain ≥ 30s K8s grace → SIGKILL mid-request",
            "Never closing ClientSession/AsyncClient → ==Unclosed== warnings, leaked sockets",
            "Untracked fire-and-forget tasks → never cancelled, shutdown hangs"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Catching Slow Callbacks",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "asyncio.run(main(), debug=True)",
            "lp = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "lp.slow_callback_duration = 0.05",
            "# logs: Executing <Task..> took",
            "#   0.312 seconds"
          ],
          "note": "same as PYTHONASYNCIODEBUG=1"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Handling SIGTERM Yourself",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "stop = asyncio.Event()",
            "lp = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "lp.add_signal_handler(",
            "    signal.SIGTERM, stop.set)",
            "await stop.wait()  # then drain"
          ],
          "note": "Unix only; uvicorn does this already"
        },
